Appendix A. Notation and Measure‑Theoretic Setup

All probabilistic arguments are grounded in a complete probability space (\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P}) equipped with a filtration \{\mathcal{F}_t\}_{t \ge 0}. The \sigma-algebra \mathcal{F}_t represents the full system history up to decision epoch t. Every random object introduced in the dissertation is adapted to this filtration.

Decision epoch. At epoch t \in \mathbb{N}, the system observes the environment state, agents propose actions, and a single action may be executed or blocked. Agent proposals, confidences, and verdicts are \mathcal{F}_t-measurable; the trust weights w_i used by the consensus layer are \mathcal{F}_{t-1}-measurable—they are fixed before the votes at epoch t are observed.

Action space and ground truth. The action set Y is finite. An oracle predicate \phi_{\text{true}} : Y \to \{0,1\} satisfies \phi_{\text{true}}(y)=1 iff y is the unique correct action, denoted y_{\text{true}}. If no such element exists, the task is ill‑posed and the system aborts.

Agent model. Agent i is described by:

· an adversarial status \iota_i \in \{0,1\} (latent, possibly adaptively chosen);
· for non‑adversarial agents (\iota_i = 0), an intrinsic error probability e_i \in [0,1) such that, conditionally on \mathcal{F}_{t-1} and \iota_i = 0, the correctness indicator Z_i := \mathbb{1}[Y_i = y_{\text{true}}] is a Bernoulli variable with success probability 1-e_i, independent across agents;
· an action proposal Y_i : \Omega \to Y and a self‑reported confidence p_i \in [0,1], both \mathcal{F}_t-measurable.

Calibration. Agent i is \gamma_i-calibrated if almost surely

\bigl|\mathbb{P}(Y_i = y_{\text{true}} \mid p_i) - p_i\bigr| \le \gamma_i

for some \gamma_i \in [0,1). Perfect calibration corresponds to \gamma_i = 0.

Key symbols (see also the Glossary in Appendix H):

\begin{aligned}
C(y) &= \sum_{i=1}^n w_i p_i \mathbb{1}[Y_i = y], \quad y^* = \arg\max_{y\in Y} C(y), \\
V_{\text{cons}}(y^*) &= \mathbb{1}[C(y^*) \ge \tau] \quad (\tau \in (1/2,1]), \\
M_\pi &= (S, s_0, \to, L) \quad (\text{Kripke structure of plan } \pi), \\
\varphi &= \Box\psi \in \Phi_{\text{safe}}, \quad V_{\text{form}}(\varphi,\pi) \in \{0,1\}, \\
R(\tau_{0:t}) &\in \{\top,\bot,?\}, \quad \kappa(y) = (V_{\text{cons}}, V_{\text{form}}, V_{\text{rt}}).
\end{aligned}

