Appendix G. Cost Model Details (Chapter 8.3)

· Consensus layer: Computing C(y) for each candidate requires summing n terms, for a total of O(n|Y|) operations per epoch. With |Y| bounded, this is O(n).
· Model checking (offline): For propositional \psi, the Büchi automaton has O(|\psi|) states; the product M_\pi \otimes \mathcal{B}_{\neg\varphi} has size O(|S|\cdot|\psi|) and emptiness is checked in linear time. For \psi with nested past operators, the automaton may grow to 2^{O(|\psi|)}, leading to PSPACE worst‑case complexity.
· Runtime monitor (online): A finite‑state machine with at most 2^{|\mathrm{AP}|} states; transition lookup per step is O(1).
· Bayesian update (online): Two parameter updates per agent, O(n) overall, or O(1) per agent.

