Appendix H. Standard Probabilistic Tools

Hoeffding’s inequality (Hoeffding 1963). Let X_1,\dots,X_m be independent random variables with a_i \le X_i \le b_i almost surely. Then for every \epsilon > 0,

\mathbb{P}\!\left( \sum_{i=1}^m (X_i - \mathbb{E}[X_i]) \ge \epsilon \right)
\le \exp\!\left( -\frac{2\epsilon^2}{\sum_{i=1}^m (b_i - a_i)^2} \right),

and the same bound holds for the lower tail.

Beta‑Binomial conjugacy. If p \sim \text{Beta}(\alpha,\beta) and S \mid p \sim \text{Binomial}(n, p), then the posterior distribution is p \mid S \sim \text{Beta}(\alpha+S,\; \beta+n-S), with mean (\alpha+S)/(\alpha+\beta+n).

Fréchet–Hoeffding bounds. For any two events A,B,

\max(0,\; \mathbb{P}(A)+\mathbb{P}(B)-1) \le \mathbb{P}(A \cap B) \le \min(\mathbb{P}(A),\mathbb{P}(B)).

